1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,380
麦琪:还没有迈克的消息吗?我要去报警.
Maggie: Still no sign of Mike? I'm going to call the police.

2
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:09,740
杰森:你说什么?现在是凌晨三点,
Jason: And what are you going to say?

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,400
我们18岁的儿子还没有回家?
It's three am and our 18 year old son isn't home yet?

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,500
麦琪:你说对了,说对了,上帝还让他进了大学.
Maggie: Your right, your right, he's in junior college for god's sakes.

5
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:22,140
杰森:对的,他不再是个孩子了.
Jason: That's right. It's not like he's a baby anymore.

6
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:27,520
麦琪,如果你不去报警的话,
Maggie, if you are not going to call the police , I will.

7
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,980
我去.你知道我真的认为这一切都是因我而起
You know I really thought all this was behind us now...and...

8
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:32,240
迈克:你们好.
Mike: Hi guys.

9
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,200
杰森和麦琪:你好,迈克 迈克????
Jason and Maggie: Hi Mike...MIKE????

10
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,040
杰森:等一下,你去哪儿了?现在应该去学校.
Jason: Wait a minute, where have you been? It's a school night.

11
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:39,200
麦琪:我们被你吓倒了.
Maggie: We were terrified something happened to you.

12
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,200
迈克:什么也没发生 晚安.
Mike: Well, nothing did... Good night.

13
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:43,860
杰森:迈克,坐……过来,
Jason: Mike, sit... Come on,

14
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:45,660
我们想知道自从上次课之后,你去哪儿了.
we want to know where you've been since your last class.

15
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:48,620
迈克:好的,我很抱歉.
Mike: All right, I'm sorry, I didn't plan on being this late.

16
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,340
我没打算这么晚的.车坏了,这可不是我的错.
It's not my fault that the lift broke.

17
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,440
杰森:好,我们不管谁犯了错.什么车?
Jason: Look, we don't care who's fault....What lift?

18
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:53,680
迈克:哦,滑雪车.
Mike: Oh the ski lift.

19
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:55,500
麦琪:你们为什么会在滑雪车上?
Maggie: Why were you on a ski lift?

20
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:58,900
迈克:你想让我怎么办,妈妈?步行上雪山?
Mike: Well what would you want me to do mom? Walk up the ski slopes?

21
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:03,060
杰森:我们希望你大学的时候在阿尔卑斯山上,不是雪山,
Jason: We want you to be on Alps land in junior college mike, not on slopes.

22
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,120
什么雪山?
What slopes?

23
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:05,840
迈克:哦,那有区别吗,爸爸?
Mike: Oh come on, does it really matter dad?

24
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:06,600
麦琪:是的,你去了哪儿?
Maggie: Yes, where did you go?

25
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,000
迈克:北部.
Mike: North.

26
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:10,900
杰森:更具体一些,迈克.
Jason: We'd like a little more to go on, Mike.

27
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:12,600
迈克:好吧,我去了普拉茨德湖.
Mike: Ok, I went to Lake Placid.

28
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:16,820
麦琪:迈克,普拉茨德湖离这超过两百里.
Maggie: Mike, lake placid is over two hundred miles away.

29
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,740
迈克:这是我晚的另一个理由.你们想让我做什么?
Mike: Which is another reason why I'm so late.

30
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:22,320
收到一张超速罚单?
What do you guys want me to do? Get a speeding ticket?

31
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,700
杰森:好了,迈克.
Jason: All right, let's cut the tap dance Mike...

32
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:25,760
迈克:爸爸……一切都很好,
Mike: Dad, dad, dad...

33
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:27,880
我在大学里,
all right look, I was at college,

34
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,140
和另外两个家伙讨论哲学,
and me and a couple of the other guys were hanging out at "landonware"

35
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:36,200
以及他们在雪季第一次去普拉茨德湖时的舢板.
discussing philosophy and junk like that when somebody mentioned that

36
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,880
因为我下午没课,
they got the first seasons snow on lake placid.

37
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,360
所以我们决定……
So since I didn't have an afternoon class, we decided to...

38
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:42,220
杰森:你星期三有社会学课.
Jason: You have sociology on Wednesdays.

39
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:44,300
迈克:不,
Mike: No no no, I dropped that duffus class weeks ago.

40
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:49,060
不不,我几个星期前放弃了这门课,
So anyway, I'm on my way up the lift for the last run of the day

41
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:50,440
所以我是在回家前的最后一节课后去了雪山.
before we head home and boom.

42
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,980
整个的雪情很严重,
This whole snowman just falls on the tow chain,

43
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:55,080
把我们捆在了半山腰,因此我进退两难,
and it stops us dead halfway up the mountain.

44
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:59,720
似乎只有被冻死的份了.
So there I am stranded, facing the very real possibility of freezing to death.

45
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:01,500
麦琪:你放弃了社会学.
Maggie: You dropped sociology.

46
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,160
迈克:是的,所以……
Mike: Yeah, so...

47
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:08,220
杰森:你认为你现在是大学生了,就可以想做什么就能做什么,
Jason: And you think that now your in college, you can do whatever you like,

48
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,420
来去自由.我没问题了.
come and go whenever you like, no questions asked.

49
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:12,100
迈克:太好了.
Mike: Pretty much, yeah.

50
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:16,900
杰森:现在能指望你五个小时以后清醒地去上经济学课程吗?
Jason: Now how do you expect to be awake for economics in 5 hours?

51
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:20,620
迈克:爸爸,我不是你所想的不负责任,
Mike: Dad, I'm not nearly as irresponsible as you think.

52
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,800
只是如此从凑巧,我也放弃了那门课.所以无论如何……
It just so happens that I dropped that class too. So anyway...

53
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:27,840
麦琪:你放弃了两门课,却不告诉我们?
Maggie: So you dropped two classes, without even telling us?

54
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:30,060
迈克:妈妈,我不想隐瞒你.
Mike: Mom, its not like I'm keeping it from you.

55
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,780
我的意思是,嘿,
I mean hey, college doesn't mind if I drop a class here or there.

56
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:38,060
大学里不介意我是否放弃一门课.爸爸,甚至有一个教授告诉我,
Dad, I even have got a professor who told me if I didn't care about his

57
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,180
如果我对他的课不感兴趣,可以不用来.
class, don't come.

58
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,540
杰森:好,你被关禁闭了.
Jason: That's it, you're grounded.

59
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:46,420
迈克:我怎么了?
Mike: I'm what?

60
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:51,600
杰森:禁闭,记住,禁闭?没有约会,没有聚会,没有生活.
Jason: Grounded. Remember, grounded? No dates, no parties, no life.

61
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,020
迈克:爸爸,你不能关一个18岁大学生的禁闭.
Mike: Dad, you cannot ground an 18 year old college man.

62
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,440
杰森:我没有.我只是关一个18岁的滑雪笨蛋.
Jason: I'm not, I'm grounding an 18 year old ski bomb.

63
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,280
迈克:不,爸爸,禁闭只能用于小孩子.
Mike: But dad, grounding is for kids.

64
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,920
杰森:事实上你就是.
Jason: Well that's exactly what you are.

65
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,020
迈克:妈妈,你能相信他对我说什么了吗?
Mike: Mom could you believe he just said that to me?

66
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:12,040
我,是一个已经足够为国效力的成年人.
To me, a guy old enough to die for his country.

67
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:15,220
麦琪:也许他应该早就如此.
Maggie: Maybe sooner than he thinks.

68
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:18,420
迈克:我不明白,这究竟怎么回事?
Mike: I don't get this, what the heck is going on around here?

69
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,520
杰森:我们只想让你表现得像一个成年人,迈克.
Jason: We just want you to behave like the adult that you are Mike.

70
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,860
迈克:哦,你现在承认我是一个成年人.
Mike: Oh so now you admit that im an adult.

71
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,560
杰森:是的,我只是按照你的说法.
Jason: Well, let me put it to you this way, all right?

72
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:29,400
只要你住在这里,你就得按我的规矩办.
As long as you live under this roof, you live under my rules

73
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:30,000
麦琪:我们的规矩.
Maggie: Our rules.

74
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:30,700
杰森:对.
Jason: Yes.

75
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,600
迈克:好了,也许我不会再住在这个屋檐下.
Mike: Well, then, fine, then maybe I won't live under this roof.

76
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:33,900
杰森:很好.
Jason: Fine.

77
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:34,600
迈克:很好.
Mike: Fine.

78
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:37,900
杰森:很好.
Jason: Fine.

79
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:43,920
迈克:很好,从明天开始.
Mike: Fine, starting tomorrow.

80
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,900
迈克:想一下,本,爸爸的主要弱点是什么?
Mike: Think about it Ben, what is dad's major weakness?

81
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:35,400
本:昂贵的理发花费.
Ben: Expensive haircuts?

82
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:37,000
迈克:不不不,我是说主要的.
Mike: No no no, I said major.

83
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,400
本:嗯……妈妈!
Ben: Uhh...Mom!

84
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:50,600
迈克:对!看,妈妈不想让我出去挨冻,这会让爸爸屈服.我相信连一个晚上的时间都不用花.实际上如果妈妈让我走出这个大门,我会很吃惊的.然后爸爸会求我留下来.
Mike: Right. See, mom will send me out there freezing and get dad to cave in. I bet it wouldn't even take a whole night. In fact I'd be surprised if mom even lets me get out the front door. And then dad will beg me to stay, on my terms.

85
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,800
本:喔.
Ben: Wow.

86
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:55,200
迈克:如果我现在不斗争的话,爸爸就会一辈子像对待小孩子一样对待我,
Mike: If I don't take a stand now, dad is just going to treat me like a kid my whole life.

87
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:59,900
杰森:如果我们现在妥协,他会永远像个小孩子.
Jason: Look, if we don't take a stand now, he will act like a kid his whole life

88
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,200
麦琪:杰森,你难道不过分吗?
Maggie: Jason, aren't you being a tad irrational?

89
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,500
杰森:你怎么能这样说?
Jason: How could you say that?

90
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:07,000
麦琪:好,你想过这样会伤害本和开萝尔吗?
Maggie: Ok well have you thought about how this could traumatize Ben and Carol?

91
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,600
开萝尔:我去布置餐桌.
Carol: I'm going to set the dinner table.

92
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,900
麦琪:谢谢你,开萝尔!
Maggie: Thank you Carol.

93
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:15,500
开萝尔:我可以坐在迈克坐的位置上吗,现在他已经是历史了?
Carol: Can I sit where Mike used to sit, now that's he's history?

94
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,600
杰森:当然,为什么不?
Jason: Sure, why not?

95
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:19,000
开萝尔:太好了.
Carol: Great.

96
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,100
杰森:开萝尔看起来很能忍耐.
Jason: Carol seems to be bearing up rather well.

97
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:24,600
麦琪:杰森,他在哪儿?
Maggie: Jason where will he live?

98
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:30,700
杰森:我告诉你,麦琪,这里!他现在还在猪圈里.
Jason: I will tell you Maggie, Here! In the same pig sty of a room he lives in now.

99
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:31,900
麦琪:我听不懂.
Maggie: I'm not following this at all.

100
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:43,000
杰森:听着,我不想让他搬走,他也不想搬走,他想吓唬我们,麦琪.杰森?西维尔可是一个打牌的高手.
Jason: Look, I don't want him to move out, and he doesn't want to move out either. He's trying to bluff us Maggie, and I'm going to call his bluff. Jason Seaver is one savvy poker player.

101
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,400
迈克:好吧,本,你送我到大门.
Mike: Sure, Ben you can walk me to the front door.

102
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:48,900
杰森:我们需要在这个问题联合起来,你同意吗?
Jason: We need to present a united front on this one, agreed?

103
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:59,900
麦琪:好,好,好.
Maggie: Yeah yeah yeah.

104
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:03,400
迈克:我想我得和你说再见.
Mike: Well, I guess I will be seeing you.

105
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,800
杰森:再见.
Jason: Guess so.

106
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:10,200
开萝尔:餐桌布置好了.哦,爸爸,我想把迈克的房间改造成健身房,行吗?
Carol: Table is all set. Oh dad, will it also be ok if I turn Mike's room into an exercise room?

107
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:12,300
迈克:什么?
Mike: What?

108
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:14,200
杰森:好主意,宝贝.
Jason: That's a good idea honey.

109
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,300
开萝尔:谢谢.
Carol: Thanks.

110
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:17,900
迈克:你至少也得体面地等我走了以后.
Mike: You can at least have the decency to wait until the body is cold.

111
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:20,700
开萝尔:生活还得继续.
Carol: Life goes on.

112
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:22,500
杰森:迈克,你有以后的地址吗?
Jason: Mike, you have a forwarding address?

113
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:28,600
迈克:有,BLA 523.
Mike: Uh yeah, BLA 523.

114
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:32,400
杰森:什么?
Jason: What?

115
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,900
迈克:我的驾照号码.
Mike: My license plate.

116
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:34,900
麦琪:你说什么?
Maggie: Pardon me?

117
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:41,000
迈克:是的,妈妈,我要住在车里了.
Mike: Yes mother, I'm going to live in my vehicle.

118
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
麦琪:杰森,他要住在车里.
Maggie: Jason, he's going to live in his vehicle.

119
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,900
杰森:好,我相信你的车不会停在我的车道上.
Jason: Well I trust your vehicle won't be parked in my driveway.

120
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:48,600
迈克:什么?
Mike: What?

121
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,900
杰森:好,搬出去,和这房子脱离关系.
Jason: Well, moving out, generally means off the premises.

122
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:53,100
麦琪:杰森,事情有点过了.
Maggie: Jason this thing has gone too far.

123
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:53,800
杰森:麦琪?
Jason: Maggie?

124
00:07:53,800 --> 00:08:00,700
麦琪:不,迈克.你可以住在你的车里,在我的车道上.
Maggie: No, Mike...You can live in your car, on my half of the driveway.

125
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:20,900
迈克:谢谢.卧室,娱乐室,我可爱的家.
Mike: Thanks. Living room, Robus room, home sweet home.

126
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,000
开萝尔:外面很冷.
Carol: Boy is it freezing out here.

127
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,800
迈克:谢谢你告诉我这鬼天气,开萝尔,出去.
Mike: Thank you Carol for that startling weather bulletin. Get out.

128
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:29,400
开萝尔:迈克,你以为我不知道你在做什么吗?
Carol: Mike, don't you think I know what you are doing?

129
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:31,700
迈克:开萝尔,你知道你自己在做什么吗?
Mike: Carol, I don't even think you know what you are doing.

130
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:38,700
开萝尔:你根本没打算搬出去,你不过是想住在这里让爸爸内疚,然后回去而已.
Carol: You have no intention of moving out, you just want to guilt dad by living here and good off.

131
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:42,000
迈克:你真的不了解我,开萝尔?现在你给我走.
Mike: You really don't know me at all do you Carol? Now get out.

132
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:53,300
开萝尔:听着!我同意把一个大学生像小孩子那样关禁闭是愚蠢的.一个18岁的成年人应该有来去自由的权利,只要他愿意.
Carol: Look, I agree that it's silly for a college student to be grounded like some child. An 18 year old should feel free to come and go as he or she pleases.

133
00:08:53,300 --> 00:09:02,200
迈克:我懂了.你站在我这边,并不是因为我是你的哥哥而关心我,而是因为你明年也要18岁了,你也要由着性子来.
Mike: Hold on I get it. So you aren't on my side because I'm your brother and you care about me. But because you turn 18 next year and you want to grease the track for your self.

134
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:04,700
开萝尔:你也完全不了解我.
Carol: You really don't know me at all do you?

135
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:06,700
迈克:开萝尔,你的自私令我恶心.
Mike: Carol your selfishness sickens me.

136
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:19,200
开萝尔:你会懂的.我们都想让爸爸给你自由,这是所有18岁的成人应得的,我可以帮你.这里有一些好吃的,给你补充点能量.
Carol: You will get over it. The point is that we both have an interest in getting dad to give you the kind of freedom that all 18 year olds so richly deserve, and I can help. Here's some tasty treats to help keep your strength up.

137
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,700
迈克:开萝尔,这些还冻着呢.
Mike: Carol, these are still frozen.

138
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:37,500
开萝尔:发动一下汽车,把它放在发动机上,20分钟后,你就有热馄饨吃了.记住,我站在你这一边,至少在精神上.
Carol: Just start your car, set it on the engine and in 20 minutes you got hot ravioli. And just remember, I'm with you on this. In spirit, anyway.

139
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:41,100
杰森:外面很冷.有什么事情我要知道吗?
Jason: It's cold out there. Anything going on in the world I should know about?

140
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:46,300
麦琪:一个十来岁的孩子被无知的父亲驱逐,冻死了,11点的电影.
Mom: Teenage boy banished by juvenile father freezes, film at 11.

141
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:59,300
杰森:无知?麦琪,我是一个受过良好训练的心理健康师,毕业于正规医学院.每个人都可以赞成或者反对我的做法,但是不可以说我是无知.
Jason: Juvenile? Well Maggie I am a highly trained mental health practitioner schooled in the complexities of the adolescent psyche. Now one may agree or disagree with my strategy but I am being anything but juvenile.

142
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:03,700
电视:天气预报,今晚长岛将有一场大雪.
TV: The weather service is calling for a major snowfall in long island tonight

143
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:06,400
杰森:好!!
Jason: Yes!!

144
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:08,000
麦琪:我去楼上看书.
Maggie: I'm going upstairs to read.

145
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:13,900
杰森:麦琪.这儿的农民们需要这场雪.
Jason: Maggie...Come on, I meant the farmers here they need the snow.

146
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,000
麦琪:农民们?
Maggie: The farmers?

147
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:22,400
杰森:我们这地区有旱情,我想我们应该更多地考虑大家的利益,而不是我们自己.
Jason: Well there is a drought going on in this country Megan, I think we have to be concerned with people with bigger problems than our own.

148
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:26,800
麦琪:你这么干吧.
Maggie: You do that.

149
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:35,100
杰森:"你好,雪",迈克在做什么呢?
Jason: "Hello snow" What does he think he's doing anyway?

150
00:10:35,100 --> 00:11:05,400
迈克:哦,喔,下雪了!好,来得正好,我能应付得了.
Mike: Oh wow, snow! All right. I got them right where I want them. Who does he think he's dealing with anyway?

151
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:10,900
迈克:时候差不多了
Mike: Ah...it's about time...

152
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,000
麦琪:外面冷死了.
Maggie: It's freezing out here.

153
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,200
迈克:如果你让我进去,我就进去.
Mike: Oh well if you insist mom I guess I'll come inside.

154
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,400
麦琪:不,你不能进来.
Maggie: No, you can't come inside.

155
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:21,000
迈克:不?我只是很想你,妈妈.
Mike: No? Well I was only thinking of you mom.

156
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,900
麦琪:你饿吗,迈克?
Maggie: Are you hungry Mike?

157
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:27,000
迈克:哦,不.天太冷,嚼不动.
Mike: Oh no, it's too cold to chew.

158
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,100
麦琪:你说真的?
Maggie: Are you sure?

159
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:35,800
迈克:是的,哦,妈妈,你来这儿了,你最好进屋去,要不然你会冻死的.告诉爸爸,我很好.
Mike: Yeah, oh mom here. You better go inside. You'll catch your death. Oh, and tell dad that I will be fine.

160
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:42,400
麦琪:我不会告诉你爸爸,我到了外面.我就想告诉你,车库顶上的储藏室里有一个取暖器.
MOM: I can't tell your father I'm out here. I just want to tell you that there is a space heater in the storage room above the garage.

161
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:50,000
迈克:但是这会用爸爸的电.这可不行,不过还是谢谢你.
Mike: Oh but that would be using dads electricity. And that would be so wrong, but thanks anyway.

162
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:58,300
麦琪:好的,迈克,你随便怎么做吧.
Maggie: well Mike, you do what you have to do.

163
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:06,200
迈克:工作就像魔咒.
Mike: Working like a charm.

164
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:12,500
杰森:加油,迈克,理智些.宝宝怎么样了?
Jason: Come on Mike, have some sense. So how's the baby?

165
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,100
麦琪:冻死了.
Maggie: Freezing.

166
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,300
杰森:冻死了?
Jason: Freezing?

167
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,900
麦琪:我没有说冻死,我是说很好.
Maggie: I didn't mean freezing I meant fine.

168
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:21,400
杰森:她的房间里要是下雪的话,肯定会冻死.
Jason: No wonder she is freezing, it's snowing in her room.

169
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:24,700
麦琪:好了,我出去看迈克了.你骂我吧.
Maggie: All right, so I went out to check on Mike. So sue me.

170
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:31,700
杰森:宝贝,我也关心迈克,这点和你一样,但是他得接受教训,你知道,迈克……他很难吸取教训.
Jason: Honey I'm just as concerned about Mike as you are but he's got an important lesson to learn here, and you know Mike...he doesn't learn easy.

171
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:34,400
麦琪:我知道,他的牛脾气和他爸一样.
Maggie: I know, he's bull headed like his father.

172
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:48,200
杰森:你指什么?难道是我们让他逃学吗?等他到了四十岁,我们还得替他交罚单?他会去抢劫便利店,然后被捕.你有时间打官司吗,你有小宝宝,你还得工作.
Jason: Oh so what do you suggest? We just let him blow college? He will be forty years old, we will still be buying his lifts tickets. He will start knocking over convenient stores, get arrested. Do you have time for a trial, what with the new baby and work and all?

173
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:56,000
麦琪:杰森,你说的很好听.我同意我们应该惩罚一下他,但是你不能对他真诚些吗?你何必要骗他?
Maggie: Jason, you are being a whacko. Now I agree that we have to get him straightened out, but can't you just be honest with him? Do you have to trick him?

174
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:03,400
杰森:我们必须让迈克知道,无论在哪里都不能犯错,我们不能再等待了.
Jason: Well we have to send Mike a message. This is it. Make no mistake where you are, this is it, the waiting is over.

175
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:08,200
麦琪:你是在按多比兄弟的那首歌办事?
Maggie: You are basing your action on a song by the Doobie brothers?

176
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:08,900
杰森:不.
Jason: No.

177
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:11,000
麦琪:我希望不是.
Maggie: Well I hope not.

178
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:18,600
杰森:那是肯妮?罗金作的曲,迈克尔?多纳德演唱,很多人以为是多比兄弟的唱片,实际上并不是.
Jason: That is a Kenny Login's tune. Michael o Donald's sang on it, so a lot of people think it was a Doobie brother's record, but no.

179
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:19,400
麦琪:杰森!!!
Maggie: Jason!!!

180
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:24,100
杰森:好吧,我和他谈谈.
Jason: Ok, all right, I'll talk to him.

181
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:29,400
麦琪:事实上,那时肯妮?罗金作的词.
Maggie: Actually, it's a Kenny Login's tune.

182
00:13:29,400 --> 00:14:17,900
杰森:迈克?我只是想看看你好不好?好的,你知道你是个牛脾气,就像你妈.我们俩停火,怎么样?你愿意进屋和我谈谈吗?我看见你在我前面,哦,上帝!!!
Jason: Mike? I just want to be sure you are ok. Ok, fine...you know you are bull-headed, just like your mother. Look, how about we call it a cease-fire ok? How about he go inside and talk about it.... I see you are way ahead of me. OH GOD!!!

183
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:20,100
迈克:爸爸,我们沟通过了.
Mike: Dad I thought we had an understanding.

184
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:21,300
杰森:你不能住在我的屋檐下.
Jason: You can't live under my roof.

185
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:22,600
迈克:但是,但是我只是……
Mike: But dad I was just...

186
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:30,500
杰森:好啊,我一直都很担心你在大雪中……现在你在这儿,看着电视,温暖如春,不用关心外面的世界.
Jason: Oh and I was all worried about you out in the snow...and now you are here, you got the TV blasting, warm as toast, you don't have a care in the world.

187
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:35,600
迈克:爸爸,几分钟前我还在外面呢,又冷又饿,孤苦伶仃.
Mike: Well dad, I wasn't up until a minute ago, I was outside, cold and lonely and hungry.

188
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,500
伙计:比萨.
Guy: Pizza.

189
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:39,000
杰森:什么?
Jason: What?

190
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,500
迈克:爸爸,我可没订比萨.
Mike: Dad I did not order that pizza.

191
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,900
杰森:你以为我会替你付钱,那你就是在做梦.
Jason: Well if you think I'm paying for that you are nuts.

192
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:47,100
伙计:嘿,放松点,麦琪?西维尔已经付过了.
Guy: Hey relax pal, it's already paid for by Maggie Seaver.

193
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:51,800
杰森:麦琪?西维尔,那不合适……迈克,马上进去.
Jason: Maggie Seaver, well doesn't that just fit...Mike get inside right now.

194
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:53,200
迈克:爸爸,我……
Mike: Dad I...

195
00:14:53,200 --> 00:15:10,200
伙计:嘿,你们不想要了吗?我告诉你们已经付过了,小费很不错.
Guy: Well hey don't you want it? I told you it's already paid for...nice tip.

196
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:13,100
杰森:好了,迈克,我们直截了当来说吧.
Jason: All right Mike, why don't we just lay out all our cards on the table now.

197
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:13,800
迈克:好的.
Mike: Fine.

198
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:14,600
杰森:好的.
Jason: Fine.

199
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:17,900
麦琪:你们两个就这么好的,好的,没完没了吗?
Maggie: Are you two going to go through this fine-fine business again?

200
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:20,300
杰森:这是你的比萨.
Jason: Here's your pizza.

201
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:23,900
麦琪:杰森,天太冷了,他看起来又这么饿.
Maggie: Jason it was so cold, and he looked so hungry.

202
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:26,200
杰森:好的,我现在担心的最后一件事不是比萨.
Jason: Well the last thing I'm worried about right now is pizza.

203
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:29,600
本:什么比萨?
Ben: What pizza?

204
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:32,300
麦琪:本,不关你的事,回去睡觉.
Maggie: Ben this doesn't concern you, go to bed.

205
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:33,900
本:迈克还在外面吗?
Ben: Is Mike still kicked out?

206
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:35,000
杰森:迈克没有被驱逐.
Jason: Mike is not kicked out.

207
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,800
本:那么他成功了
Ben: Then It worked.

208
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:39,600
杰森:什么成功了?
Jason: What worked?

209
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:44,200
本:哦,没事,当然这不是迈克的计划.
Ben: Um nothing, certainly not Mike's plan.

210
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:52,900
杰森:迈克,你别想骗任何人,我不是傻瓜.我知道你没想过住在车里,你只是争取同情,让我屈服.
Jason: Mike you are not fooling anybody, I'm not stupid. I know you didn't intend to live in your car; you were just putting on that pathetic little act so that I cave in.

211
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:55,800
迈克:不,爸爸,我不会使用屈服这个词.
Mike: Well no dad, I would not use the term cave in.

212
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,300
开萝尔:你们在吵什么呢?你们把宝宝吵醒了.
Carol: What's all this shouting about? You guys are going to wake the baby.

213
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:01,700
麦琪:开萝尔,我们在和你的哥哥讨论事,你介意吗?
Maggie: Carol, we are having a discussion with your brother, do you mind?

214
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:13,400
开萝尔:完全可以.哦,在我上楼之前我想说些话.
Carol: Not in the least. Oh, well, before I go upstairs I want to say something.

215
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,800
麦琪:说吧,开萝尔?
Maggie: what is it Carol?

216
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:25,200
开萝尔:实际上,我看见迈克离开这房子,我很兴奋,我相信18岁的人法律上应该拥有某种不可剥夺的权力,这些是……
Carol: Well actually, as delighted as I am to see Mike out of my house, I do believe that 18 year olds is legally endowed with certain undeniable rights, and among these are...

217
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,700
杰森:你想知道我相信什么吗,开萝尔?
Jason: You want to know what I believe Carol?

218
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:27,800
开萝尔:什么?
Carol: What?

219
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:39,000
杰森:我相信你并不介意迈克的权力,你只关心明年你18岁后,你所考虑的个人自由,我说的不错吧?
Jason: I believe that you are not so concerned about Mike's rights as you are about t the fact that you are going to turn 18 next year and you're thinking about your personal freedom, now am I getting warm?

220
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:43,100
开萝尔:你一点也不了解我.
Carol: You really don't know me at all do you?

221
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,800
麦琪:晚安,开萝尔.
Maggie: Good night Carol.

222
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:48,800
迈克:很顺利,真的很顺利.
Mike: Smooth, real smooth.

223
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,400
杰森:好的,我们说到哪了?
Jason: All right where were we?

224
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:59,400
麦琪:你刚才说迈克在演戏,你知道,打牌的老手也在做同样的事情.
Maggie: Oh you were just saying that Mike was putting on an act, you know, sort of the same thing the old savvy poker player was doing?

225
00:16:59,400 --> 00:16:59,900
迈克:什么?
Mike: What?

226
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:04,400
杰森:好吧,我承认,我不想让你搬走,迈克,没有人想让你搬走.
Jason: Ok I admit it; I didn't want you to move out Mike, anymore than you wanted to move.

227
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:06,100
麦琪:终于说实话了.
Maggie: Finally the truth.

228
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:16,900
杰森:我只是不能容忍,大学第一年就虚度光阴,逃课,跳华尔兹跳到很晚,只要你乐意,让你妈妈和我担心你每天晚上会在哪儿.
Jason: I just couldn't bare to watch you just fritter away your first year in college. Dropping classes left and right or walcing in and out as late as you please, and making your mother and I worried sick about where you are every night.

229
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:28,300
迈克:首先,我没有虚度光阴,懂吗?我只是稍微调整了一下我的课程,我没有在这跳华尔兹,我甚至不知道什么是华尔兹.
Mike: Well first of all, I did not fritter, ok? I merely fined tuned my class schedule. And and I did not walce in here, I don't even know how to walce.

230
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:29,800
杰森:我受不了你这样的态度,迈克.
Jason: I can't live with you like this Mike.

231
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,700
迈克:我也受不了你的愚蠢规定,自从我刚学会走路就一直没有改变过.
Mike: And I can't live with your stupid rules because they haven't changed since I have been a toddler.

232
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,100
杰森:你不改变,它们也不会改变.
Jason: And they won't until you change.

233
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:34,700
迈克:那很好.
Mike: Well fine

234
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:35,400
杰森:很好.
Jason: Fine.

235
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:56,200
麦琪:太好了,现在我们回家说很好吧.两头牛,没有一个愿意承认对方哪怕有一点道理,杰森,这个问题上我们需要统一.
Maggie: Great, now we are back to fine. I mean 2 bull headed know-it-alls, staring each other down, neither one willing to admit that the other one just might have a point. Jason, we need to present a united front on this one.

236
00:17:56,200 --> 00:18:01,500
杰森:好了,也许对于你这么大的人,关禁闭是不合适的.
Jason: All right, uh, maybe it's not appropriate for someone your age to be grounded.

237
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:07,900
迈克:的确如此,那是我一直想说的.
Mike: Exactly, that's what I have been trying to say all along....what?

238
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:10,800
麦琪:该轮到你让一步了.
Maggie: No it's your turn to concede a point.

239
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:21,100
迈克:妈妈,我没有什么要让的.好,也许没告诉你们我在哪儿,让你们担心,是我不对.
Mike: Mom, I have nothing to concede...Ok, maybe scaring you guys by not telling you where I was, was a little wrong.

240
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:32,400
杰森:你说了它是错误的.一个大学生也许应该有一点权力自己做决定.
Jason: You bet it was wrong. And maybe a college man should have a little leeway in making his own decisions.

241
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:39,000
迈克:我应该在放弃这些课程之前找你商量一下,但是只是听一下你的建议.
Mike: And I guess I could run it by you before I drop classes, but just to hear your advice.

242
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,800
杰森:那正是我要的.
Jason: That's all I ask.

243
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:48,100
麦琪:现在我们有进展了……看,这样不很好吗?
Maggie: Now we are getting somewhere...see? Isn't this fun?

244
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:51,800
迈克:我相信你不想让你的儿子在外面挨冻.
Mike: Boy, I sure didn't think you would send your son out there to freeze.

245
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:54,700
杰森:迈克,我让你在外面挨冻的唯一理由是因为我爱你.
Jason: Mike the only reason I sent you out there to freeze was because I love you.

246
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:56,400
迈克:真想看到你如何对待一个陌生人.
Mike: Well I'd hate to see how you treat a stranger.

247
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:56,900
麦琪:迈克……
Maggie: Mike...

248
00:18:56,900 --> 00:19:02,900
杰森:如果一个陌生人搬来这儿,我才不管他去哪,他做了什么,也不管有是否逃学呢.
Jason: Well if a stranger moved in here, I wouldn't care where he went or what he did, or how he screwed up his education.

249
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:03,800
麦琪:哦,杰森.
Maggie: Oh Jason.

250
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:07,400
迈克:哦,如果一个陌生人搬到这儿,你不会指望他遵守你愚蠢的规定.
Mike: Oh yeah, well if a stranger moved in here, you wouldn't expect him to live by your stupid rules either.

251
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:09,700
杰森:不,但是我指望他付给我房租.
Jason: No, but I'd expect him to pay rent then.

252
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:11,300
迈克:好,他也不会被关禁闭.
Mike: Well, beats the heck out of being grounded.

253
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:12,600
